  "final": {
    "agentMessage": "Yes - you **can renew online in most cases**.\n\nOn the California DMV site (dmv.ca.gov):\n\n* Homepage > **“How Can We Help? Search a topic”** \n  * Searched: `driver license renewal`\n\n* Results load the **“Service Advisor – driver license renewal”** panel which states:\n\n> **Option 1**\n> **Renew online to save time. In most cases, Driver's License Renewals and ID Card Renewals are no longer processed at the DMV office and can be completed quickly and easily online.**\n\n> **Option 2**\n> *You may be eligible to renew by mail. Learn more.*\n\n> **Option 3**\n> *There are cases that require renewal in person, such as eligibility, restrictions, etc. In these cases, you may schedule an appointment to renew at the DMV office.*\n\n**Where to start the online renewal:**\n\nOn that Service Advisor result, under **Option 1** is a large blue button:\n\n**Renew Online**\n\nThat is the entry point to start online renewal. The text links in Option 1 to **“Driver's License Renewals”** and **“ID Card Renewals”** are the informational pages with full eligibility details.\n\nI did not proceed past that information screen into login/payment."
  },
